2. FORENSIC SCIENCE, LEGAL ADMISSIBILITY & ACCREDITATION DISCLAIMERS
================================================================================

2.1. ISO/IEC 17025:2017 & ENFSI / SWGDAM ACCREDITATION NOTICE:
     The Software implements computational algorithms and biostatistical models 
     (including continuous Markov Chain Monte Carlo mixture deconvolution, 
     Dirichlet population genetics, HIrisPlex-S phenotyping, epigenetic clocks, 
     3D bloodstain pattern analysis, and Zero-Knowledge Proof cryptographic verifiers) 
     derived from peer-reviewed scientific literature. However, deployment of the 
     Software in active forensic casework, law enforcement investigations, or judicial 
     proceedings MUST be preceded by formal internal laboratory developmental and 
     internal validation in accordance with ISO/IEC 17025:2017 Clause 7.2, 
     ILAC G19:08/2022, SWGDAM Guidelines for Validation of Probabilistic Genotyping 
     Systems, and ENFSI Guidelines for Evaluative Reporting in Forensic Science (2017).

2.2. EXPERT WITNESS & JUDICIAL ADMISSIBILITY:
     The biostatistical likelihood ratios (LR), random match probabilities (RMP), 
     phenotypic estimations, and geo-forensic heatmaps generated by the Software 
     are investigative tools and probabilistic computational aids. They do NOT 
     substitute for the professional judgment, peer-review, and sworn testimony 
     of a qualified forensic expert witness under Federal Rules of Evidence Rule 702, 
     the Daubert standard (509 U.S. 579), the Frye standard (293 F. 1013), or 
     corresponding national evidence admissibility laws.

2.3. PROSECUTOR'S & DEFENSE COUNSEL'S FALLACY SAFEGUARD:
     All likelihood ratios computed by the Software represent relative probabilities 
     of the forensic evidence given competing propositions P(E | Hp) / P(E | Hd) 
     and MUST NEVER be transposed or interpreted as the direct posterior probability 
     of guilt, innocence, or donor identity P(Hp | E) in the absence of independent, 
     lawful prior odds established by the trier of fact.

================================================================================
3. BIOMETRIC DATA PRIVACY & ZERO-KNOWLEDGE CRYPTOGRAPHIC GUARANTEES
================================================================================

3.1. SPECIAL CATEGORY DATA PROTECTION:
     Users of the Software are solely responsible for ensuring compliance with all 
     applicable biometric and genetic privacy statutes, including but not limited to 
     the European Union General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) Article 9 (Special 
     Categories of Data), the US Criminal Justice Information Services (CJIS) 
     Security Policy, HIPAA, and national genetic privacy laws.

3.2. ZERO-KNOWLEDGE MATCH PRIVACY:
     The Circom/Groth16 ZK-SNARK circuit implementations (BN254 curve) and Binary 
     Merkle Tree Chain of Custody modules are mathematically formulated to verify 
     genomic profile inclusion thresholds (LR >= 10^6, allele threshold matches) 
     without disclosing raw Short Tandem Repeat (STR) or Single Nucleotide Polymorphism 
     (SNP) allele designations. The zero-knowledge privacy guarantee holds under the 
     computational hardness assumptions of the Discrete Logarithm and Bilinear 
     Diffie-Hellman problems over BN254.

